From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 08:12:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: watchdog: sbsa_gwdt: stop MT8901 ping worker
 during suspend

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2169002

On MediaTek SBSA watchdogs in action=1 mode, the sleep notifier
parks the hardware watchdog, but the watchdog-core keepalive timer
remains armed. Its SYS_TIMER interrupt can wake MT8901 from S3 even
though the hardware watchdog is parked.

Use the existing watchdog-core PM hook in this mode to cancel the
ping worker during system sleep and restore it on resume. Leave
action=0 unchanged: its WS0 heartbeat workaround needs separate
resume-time accounting before its core worker can be quiesced.

Fixes: 280db0e8cf30f4003624580b5a9f0c7a96779588 ("NVIDIA: SAUCE: watchdog: sbsa_gwdt: park the watchdog around system sleep on MediaTek implementations")
Signed-off-by: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Matthew R. Ochs <mochs@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Nirmoy Das <nirmoyd@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Carol L Soto <csoto@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0bd88a1da4b3aefee1674d890e22b5d9bce6ead1 resolute:linux-nvidia-bos)
Signed-off-by: Jacob Martin <jacob.martin@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00716
Ledger-Origin: nvidia@819eb14048e6ec794431dc31c165f721c14902d4
---
 drivers/watchdog/sbsa_gwdt.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/watchdog/sbsa_gwdt.c b/drivers/watchdog/sbsa_gwdt.c
index 1e97c07141a3..bd6d1d05fe7b 100644
--- a/drivers/watchdog/sbsa_gwdt.c
+++ b/drivers/watchdog/sbsa_gwdt.c
@@ -830,6 +830,9 @@ static int sbsa_gwdt_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	 */
 	if (!gwdt->no_hw_stop)
 		watchdog_stop_on_reboot(wdd);
+	/* The action=0 WS0 workaround needs separate resume heartbeat accounting. */
+	if (gwdt->no_hw_stop && action)
+		watchdog_stop_ping_on_suspend(wdd);
 	ret = devm_watchdog_register_device(dev, wdd);
 	if (ret) {
 		if (early_action)
